From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/17] Provide host-coherent memory over the socket transport

A synthetic HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT memory type is appended after the
device's host-visible type and mapped back to it on the wire. Before every
submit, mapped coherent allocations are flushed (changed blocks only); after a
fence or queue wait, ranges the GPU wrote through transfer commands into
readback buffers are invalidated back into the guest mapping. Imageless
framebuffers carry placeholder attachments so the decoder accepts them.
